Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["How to adapt this example", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9db809da-aeea-4cc8-8d54-b2b4f09be7a1"],

Cell["\<\
Change one ingredient at a time: a mass, a momentum assignment, or a vertex \
order. Restart the kernel before rerunning with different kinematics, because \
scalar-product definitions and assumptions persist in the session. \
Re-evaluate all dependent cells after a change. Inspect the stored \
intermediate expressions if a comparison is False or remains unevaluated; do \
not treat an unresolved expression as a passed check.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a328abc8-963f-44b4-8aad-68bae7d4466c"],

Cell["\<\
References: P. van Nieuwenhuizen, Nucl. Phys. B 60 (1973) 478; A. Accioly et \
al., Int. J. Theor. Phys. 39 (2000) 1599. The algebraic conventions are those \
of the installed FeynGrav definitions displayed above.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fec076fc-8fcb-44a4-ba86-c5f151c78ab9"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
